{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1154295-various-questions-for-my-mage-game","id":1154295,"title":"Various Questions for my Mage game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-30T22:02:04-07:00","id":1154295,"title":"Various Questions for my Mage game","content":"I thought about making two separate posts since these two questions have nothing to do with each other but I will save the forums space. Ive been running a mage game for a few months set in London. One of the current plots consists of the players encountering the blood farm from Shadows over UK. In short, its vampires draining humans dry in a factory and selling the blood. Ive added on that mysteriously the vampires who run the farm have found a way to keep the blood fresh, In an attempt to resolve the problem without starting a war with the vampires, they want to use magic to create an alternative to the blood farm by producing their own blood from tass. What would you use to create blood and how much blood could they create?<br /> <br /> Second question is a bit different. Somehow I ended up with zero adamantine arrows in my group so I am trying to think of creative ways to use the adamantine arrow as antagonists or rivals. I am coming up short on why the adamantine arrow would oppose the PC cabal though. Give me ideas for BAD adamantine arrows!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T01:12:27-07:00","id":1154311,"title":"","content":"Knit is capable of healing wounds. Exsanguination kills. You could probably create a certain amount of blood with the spell, or at least another perfecting Life spell. That being said, the game isn't really about scientific measurements of the effects of the spells, but rather the narrative effects. Far more importantly than how much blood could a Life mage make would be all the questions surrounding basic interaction with the vampires: questions like &quot;Is it REALLY a safe idea to have ANY kind of deals with vampires other than marking each side's territory and vowing not to cross into their territory?&quot;, &quot;Maybe we can study their magic (aka supernatural abilities) without being near them at all. We just need an apprentice of Space, even better if the person has even more skill or has the spell as a rote,&quot; or &quot;What are we getting out of this deal apart from not starting a war? If we are going to give a commodity that other, nastier, vampires would kill to have, we need more than a lack of threats of war, we need something big too. Like, LOTS of magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> Bullies as sentinels. Sentinels are often Arrows or Guardians.<br /> Arrows that are constantly challenging your group to competitions that are in their favor.<br /> Arrows that have caused several really nasty paradoxes and aren't stopping because they MUST get that set of super spells off.<br /> Arrows that have killed several people, at least one of them being someone important (not necessarily blood related) to the pcs.<br /> Arrows forcing others to take public Vows (vows enforced by Fate magic). One nasty twist is to have an arrow changing the terms of the vows.<br /> Arrows delving deeply into politics and mucking about with the laws of the consilium to benefit themselves (or at least one powerful arrow).<br /> <br /> Those are probably some more cliche/archetypal examples. I imagine that most other people here on these forums could come up with something a bit more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T03:08:14-07:00","id":1154323,"title":"","content":"Let there be a high ranking arrow who tailors his approach to conflict more in the way of a chessmaster than a bruiser and who schemes to keep the consilium healthy by causing conflict that keeps everyone sharp and gets rid of undesireables. One of these undesireables happens to be a pcs mentor or the pcs themselves.<br /> <br /> If you want more straight up villains... well there are the devourers of the flesh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1154295-various-questions-for-my-mage-game?p=1154311#post1154311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One nasty twist is to have an arrow changing the terms of the vows.</div> </div> </div> </div>While definitly possible I want to point out that doing so would go against the code of the arrows, meaning whoever did it would be a rouge in the eyes of his own order. The Arrow holds Oaths sacred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":5241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","user":"Flinty","date":". 10-31-2017, 06:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T03:15:09-07:00","id":1154324,"title":"","content":"Arrows:<br /> * Who are fighting a threat and don't have any compunctions against conscripting others to fight some battles against their will.<br /> * That have largely taken a vow to act as enforcers of the PCs rivals. It is just Business.<br /> * That buy into the &quot;whatever doesn't kill you, makes you stronger&quot; philosophy way too much, and deliberately cause problems (&quot;trials&quot;) for other Mages to &quot;strengthen&quot; them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T03:25:14-07:00","id":1154327,"title":"","content":"You could link the two plots together. Sure, the PCs don't want a war with the vampires, but the Arrow might be up for it. I mean, the blood farm must have logistical links with the major kindred population centres, therefore there'd be ready made intel on where Elysiums are.<br /> <br /> Hell, the Arrow could plan to mess with the blood in some way. There are some nasty kindred specific infections, the Red Worms from Intruders come to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T10:18:24-07:00","id":1154431,"title":"","content":"If the what you want is a hostile Arrow without undermining or changing the way the Order works then watch Bruce Willis in The Siege.<br /> \u200bStart hostilities with the Vampires, think of them as the opening salvos of a coming war, then set the Arrow loose to protect Mage society with more than necessary and often obstructionist gusto.<br /> Martial Law looks ugly from the view of those under it, especially when told that it is for their own good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T11:09:53-07:00","id":1154447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1154295-various-questions-for-my-mage-game?p=1154431#post1154431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the what you want is a hostile Arrow without undermining or changing the way the Order works then watch Bruce Willis in The Siege.<br /> \u200bStart hostilities with the Vampires, think of them as the opening salvos of a coming war, then set the Arrow loose to protect Mage society with more than necessary and often obstructionist gusto.<br /> Martial Law looks ugly from the view of those under it, especially when told that it is for their own good.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you want to veer them (or at least an influential member) into Villain Territory, you can make it so they secretly started hostilities as a way to increase their own importance/power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T17:16:59-07:00","id":1154551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1154295-various-questions-for-my-mage-game?p=1154447#post1154447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And if you want to veer them (or at least an influential member) into Villain Territory, you can make it so they secretly started hostilities as a way to increase their own importance/power.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOr have it be a member who sees Vampires as a great evil that must be wiped out and he will do whatever it takes to get the rest of the Consillium on board.<br /> Racism doesn't see itself as evil but simply trying to protect their own. A flaw that seems very appropriate to the Arrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T17:38:36-07:00","id":1154563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1154295-various-questions-for-my-mage-game?p=1154551#post1154551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bOr have it be a member who sees Vampires as a great evil that must be wiped out and he will do whatever it takes to get the rest of the Consillium on board.<br /> Racism doesn't see itself as evil but simply trying to protect their own. A flaw that seems very appropriate to the Arrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fun part is, there isn't a reason why it can't be both - a manipulator who wants power, and someone who wants to &quot;strike first&quot;. Maybe one is using the other, maybe they never could have done it individually, whatever. Options!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T19:49:26-07:00","id":1154585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1154295-various-questions-for-my-mage-game?p=1154563#post1154563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fun part is, there isn't a reason why it can't be both - a manipulator who wants power, and someone who wants to &quot;strike first&quot;. Maybe one is using the other, maybe they never could have done it individually, whatever. Options!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Heck, they could both be the same person. Someone who legit thinks that vampires are awful, but wouldn't shrink from using the incident to get more power to leverage for their other interests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T22:57:43-07:00","id":1154634,"title":"","content":"Wow these ideas are awesome. This session the players dug themselves in deeper so all of this will be useful. I think I want a manipulator Adamantine arrow that will be attempting to increase hostilities to undermine the Guardian of the Veil Hierarch. The players havnt fully thought through the possible consequences of creating an alternative blood source for the vampires, but I think that this is a good theme of mage where power comes with real unintended consequences that the players in their hubris may regret. I am also going to create a variety of adamantine arrow npcs with all these different adamantine arrow problems to create a variety of more personal dilemmas for my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T05:25:15-07:00","id":1154670,"title":"","content":"Depending on how villainous a brush you want to paint the Arrow with, remember to include a few sympathetic Arrows as well - maybe one honorable, but by-the-book or loyal to the hierarchy (so the PCs can't trust them with any real secrets, or extract secret info from - at least without trickery).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T19:30:05-08:00","id":1156543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flinty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1154295-various-questions-for-my-mage-game?p=1154323#post1154323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While definitly possible I want to point out that doing so would go against the code of the arrows, meaning whoever did it would be a rouge in the eyes of his own order. The Arrow holds Oaths sacred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, yeah, hence BAD GUY Arrow. Any member of any order that is willing to break the traditions and rules of their order to benefit themselves is kind of by definition a bad guy. Or at least a very unscrupulous and selfish person.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}